  "question": {
    "text": "A physical quantity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>S</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;is defined as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>S</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></math>. where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;is electric field,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;is magnetic field and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is the permeability of free space. The dimensions of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>S</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;are the same as the dimensions of which of the following quantity/quantities?",
    "image": null
  },
